From 4f1c1b7d2f9a4e0c8b3d5a6f7e8d9c0b1a2b3c4d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: jacksongoode <jacksongoode@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 12:00:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Kompakt: frame rate divisor from
 persist.sys.kompakt.fps_divisor

Choreographer can already skip frames -- setFPSDivisor, which AOSP uses for its
own low FPS experiments -- but only debug.hwui.fps_divisor reaches it, and no
setting can write that.

The divisor now also comes from persist.sys.kompakt.fps_divisor, which the
Kompakt app can set. Unset, it falls back to the debug property, so a build
without the app behaves as stock.

Input is not affected: ViewRootImpl runs a touch on the UI thread as it arrives,
not through the Choreographer, so the cap only holds back the draw. The
batched-motion path does divide, which samples a drag at the capped rate.
---
 core/java/android/view/Choreographer.java | 4 +++-
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/core/java/android/view/Choreographer.java b/core/java/android/view/Choreographer.java
index 3a2ec91..9cd5931 100644
--- a/core/java/android/view/Choreographer.java
+++ b/core/java/android/view/Choreographer.java
@@ -350,7 +350,9 @@ public final class Choreographer {
             mCallbackQueues[i] = new CallbackQueue();
         }
         // b/68769804: For low FPS experiments.
-        setFPSDivisor(SystemProperties.getInt(ThreadedRenderer.DEBUG_FPS_DIVISOR, 1));
+        // Kompakt: the Display tab's frame rate cap is this same divisor.
+        setFPSDivisor(SystemProperties.getInt("persist.sys.kompakt.fps_divisor",
+                SystemProperties.getInt(ThreadedRenderer.DEBUG_FPS_DIVISOR, 1)));
     }
 
     private static float getRefreshRate() {
